  "title": "71: Nooh نوح",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖۤ اَنْ اَنْذِرْ قَوْمَكَ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(1)\nINNAA ARSALNAA ARSALNAA ELAA QAWMEHI AN AANZER QAWMAKA MIN QABLE AN YYAATEEHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nVerily, sent We Noah unto his people, saying: “Warn then thy people? ere cometh there upon them a painful chastisement\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(2)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI INNEE LAKUM NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nSaid he: “O’ ye my people! Verily, I am unto you an open warner!\nاَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَاتَّقُوْهُ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِۙ‏(3)\nSAALEHAN BODUL LAAHA WAT TAQOOHO WAATEEU’OONE.\nThat worship ye God (alone), Fear Him, and Obey me\nيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ مِّنْ ذُنُوْبِكُمْ وَيُؤَخِّرْكُمْ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّىؕ اِنَّ اَجَلَ اللّٰهِ اِذَا جَآءَ لَا يُؤَخَّرُۘ لَوْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(4)\nYAGHFER LAKUM MIN ZUNOOBEKUM WAYUAKKHERKUM ELAA ELAA MOSAMMAA INNAL AJALAL LAAHE EZAA JAAA-A LAA YUAKKHARU LAW KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nHe will forgive you of your sins and respite you unto an appointed term; Verily, the term (fixed) of God, when it cometh, shall not be put back, if ye but knew (this)!\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ دَعَوْتُ قَوْمِىْ لَيْلًا وَّنَهَارًا ۙ‏(5)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE DAA’AWTU QAWMEE LAYLAN WWANAHAARAN.\nSaid he: “O’ my Lord! Verily I called my people by night and by day!\nفَلَمْ يَزِدْهُمْ دُعَآءِىْۤ اِلَّا فِرَارًا‏(6)\nFALAM YAZEDHUM DUA’AAEAA ILLAA FERAARAA.\nBut increased not (for) them my call but (their) flight (from the Right Way)\nوَاِنِّىْ كُلَّمَا دَعَوْتُهُمْ لِتَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ جَعَلُوْۤا اَصَابِعَهُمْ فِىْۤ اٰذَانِهِمْ وَاسْتَغْشَوْا ثِيَابَهُمْ وَاَصَرُّوْا وَاسْتَكْبَرُوا اسْتِكْبَارًا ۚ‏(7)\nWA INNEE KULLAMAA DAA’AWTUHUM LETAGHFERA LAHUM JAA’ALOOA ASAABE-A’HUM FEE AAZAANEHIM WAASTAGHSHAWA SEEABAHUM WAASARROOA WAASTAKBAROOA ASTEKBAARAN.\nWhenever I called them, that Thou mayest forgive them, they thrust their fingers into their ears, and covered themselves in their garments, and persist (in their error), and are puffed with pride\nثُمَّ اِنِّىْ دَعَوْتُهُمْ جِهَارًا ۙ‏(8)\nSUMMA INNEE DAA’AWTUHUM JEHAARAN.\nThen verily I called unto them aloud (too)\nثُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَعْلَنْتُ لَهُمْ وَاَسْرَرْتُ لَهُمْ اِسْرَارًا ۙ‏(9)\nSUMMA INNEE AAA’LANTU LAHUM WAASRARTU LAHUM AESRAARAN.\nThen verily spake I openly unto them, and I confided unto them in secret (too)\nفَقُلْتُ اسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ غَفَّارًا ۙ‏(10)\nFA-QULTUS STAGHFEROO RABBAKUM, INNAHU KAANA GHAFFAARAANY.\nThen said I: “Seek ye the forgiveness of your Lord! Verily He is the Most-Forgiving\nيُّرْسِلِ السَّمَآءَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّدْرَارًا ۙ‏(11)\nYURSELIS SAMAA-A A’LAYKUM MIDRAARAANW.\nHe will send (down) upon you the cloud raining in torrents\nوَّيُمْدِدْكُمْ بِاَمْوَالٍ وَّبَنِيْنَ وَيَجْعَلْ لَّكُمْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّيَجْعَلْ لَّكُمْ اَنْهٰرًا ؕ‏(12)\nWA YUMDIDKUM BE-AMWAALINW WA BANEENA WA YAJ-A’L LAKUM JANNAATINW WA YAJ-A’L LAKUM ANHAARAA.\nAnd help you with wealth and sons (children) and make (grow) for you gardens, and make for you rivers\nمَا لَكُمْ لَا تَرْجُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ وَقَارًا ۚ‏(13)\nMAA LAKUM LAA TARJOONA LILLAAHE WAQAARAN.\nWhat hath happened unto you that ye consider not for God any greatness?\nوَقَدْ خَلَقَكُمْ اَطْوَارًا‏(14)\nWA QAD KHALAQAKUM AATWAARAN.\nWhile indeed He created you through regular stages\nاَلَمْ تَرَوْا كَيْفَ خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ سَبْعَ سَمٰوٰتٍ طِبَاقًا ۙ‏(15)\nALAM TARAWA KAYFA KHALAQAL LAAHO SAB-A’ SAMAAWAATIN TEBAAQAN.\nSee ye not how hath created God the seven heavens (in layers) one above the other?\nوَّجَعَلَ الْقَمَرَ فِيْهِنَّ نُوْرًا ۙ وَّجَعَلَ الشَّمْسَ سِرَاجًا‏(16)\nANHAARAWN WA LAL FEEHINNA NOORAN ANHAARAWN SHAMSA SERAAJANW.\nAnd made the moon, in it a light, and the sun as a lamp\nوَاللّٰهُ اَنْۢبَتَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ نَبَاتًا ۙ‏(17)\nWAL LAAHO AANBATAKUM MENAL ARZE NABAATAN.\nAnd God made you grow of the earth as a growth (of a plant)\nثُمَّ يُعِيْدُكُمْ فِيْهَا وَيُخْرِجُكُمْ اِخْرَاجًا‏(18)\nSUMMA YUE’EEDUKUM FEEHAA WAYUKHREJUKUM AEKHRAAJAN.\nThen He returneth you therein, and again will He bringeth you forth a new’ bringing (at the Resurrection)\nوَاللّٰهُ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ بِسَاطًا ۙ‏(19)\nWAL LAAHO JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA BESAATAN.\nAnd verily God hath made for you the earth outstretched\nلِّتَسْلُكُوْا مِنْهَا سُبُلًا فِجَاجًا‏(20)\nLLETASLUKOOA MINHAA SUBULAN FEJAAJAN.\nThat ye may walk therein along paths wide (convenient)\nقَالَ نُوْحٌ رَّبِّ اِنَّهُمْ عَصَوْنِىْ وَاتَّبَعُوْا مَنْ لَّمْ يَزِدْهُ مَالُهٗ وَوَلَدُهٗۤ اِلَّا خَسَارًا ۚ‏(21)\nQAALA NOOHUN RABBIL INNAHUM A’ASAWNEAA WAT TABA-O’O MAN LAM YAZEDHU MAALOHU WAWALADUH ILLAA KHASAARAN.\nSaid Noah: “O’ my Lord! They have disobeyed me, but follow they him whose riches and children increase not unto him but loss\nوَمَكَرُوْا مَكْرًا كُبَّارًا ۚ‏(22)\nWA MAKAROO MAKRAWN KUBBAARAN.\nAnd they have plotted a great plot\nوَ قَالُوْا لَا تَذَرُنَّ اٰلِهَتَكُمْ وَلَا تَذَرُنَّ وَدًّا وَّلَا سُوَاعًا  ۙ وَّ لَا يَغُوْثَ وَيَعُوْقَ وَنَسْرًا ۚ‏(23)\nWA QAALOO LAA TAZARUNNA AAALEHATAKUM WA LAA TAZARUNNA WADDAN WA LAA SOOAA’AN WA LAA YAGHOOSA WAYAU’OOQA WANASRAN.\nAnd say they (unto each other) -. “Forsake not ye your gods, and forsake not Wadd, nor Suwa; neither Yaghus, and Ya’uq and Nasr!\nوَقَدْ اَضَلُّوْا كَثِيْرًا  ۚ وَلَا تَزِدِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ اِلَّا ضَلٰلًا‏(24)\nWA QAD AAZALLOOA KASEERAA WA LAA TAZEDE ZAALEMEEN ILLAA ZALAALAM.\nAnd indeed, have they led astray many, and then increase not unto the unjust (aught) but error\nمِّمَّا خَطِٓيْئٰتِهِمْ اُغْرِقُوْا فَاُدْخِلُوْا نَارًا  ۙ فَلَمْ يَجِدُوْا لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَنْصَارًا‏(25)\nMIMMAA KHATEEEAATEHEM AUGHREQOOA FAADKHELOOA NAARAN FALAM YAJEDOOA LAHUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE AANSAARAN.\nBecause of their (own) sins they were drowned, and were made to enter the fire, and (then) they found not any helper for them besides God\nوَ قَالَ نُوْحٌ رَّبِّ لَا تَذَرْ عَلَى الْاَرْضِ مِنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ دَيَّارًا‏(26)\nWA QAALA NOOHUN RABBIL LAA TAZAR A’LAL ARZE MENAL KAAFEREEN DAYARAN.\nAnd said Noah! “O’ my Lord! leave Thou not on the earth, of the unjust ones, a single dweller (alive)?\nاِنَّكَ اِنْ تَذَرْهُمْ يُضِلُّوْا عِبَادَكَ وَلَا يَلِدُوْۤا اِلَّا فَاجِرًا كَفَّارًا‏(27)\nINNAKA IN TAZARHUM YUZELLOOA E’EBAADAKA WA LAA YALEDOOA ILLAA FAAJERAN KAFFAARAN.\nVerily if Thou leaveth them (alive), they will lead astray Thy servants, and will not beget they but immoral ingrates!\nرَبِّ اغْفِرْلِىْ وَلِوَالِدَىَّ وَلِمَنْ دَخَلَ بَيْتِىَ مُؤْمِنًا وَّلِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنٰتِؕ وَلَا تَزِدِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ اِلَّا تَبَارًا‏(28)\nRABBE AGHFERLEAA WALEWAALEDAA WA LEMAN DAKHALA BAYTEYA MUMENAN WWALELMUMENEENA MOA-MENAAT WA WA LAA TAZEDE ZAALEMEEN ILLAA TABAARAN.\nO’ my Lord! Forgive Thou me and my parents and him who entereth my abode believing (in Thee), and the believer- men and the believer-women, and increase not unto the unjust ones in aught save perdition!",
  "merits": "Surah Nooh\nThis Surah has 28 verses and it is ‘Makki’. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that those who recite this Surah will get a reward equal to the number of people who believe in Prophet Nuh (a.s.).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that those who believe in Allah (s.w.t.), His Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and recite the Holy Qur’an, should never leave out Surah Nooh as they will gain a place among the favoured servants of Allah (s.w.t.) by reciting it. He will get three places in Jannah instead of one and he will be given 200 houries. Any supplications made after reciting this Surah are quickly answered. The one who recites this Surah often will not die until he sees his place in Jannah."
